I've read a lot on this newsgroup about how tough the major (namded) demons
are in 3.1.  So, I enter Gehennum with my trusty blessed +3 Vorpal Blade.
Asmodeus asks for 19457 gold pieces (for safe passage).  This is, of course,
unacceptable to me.  I offer him -57 instead.  (fortunately, the dev team
was very creative about this ... good job!)  It says "You attempt to short-
change Asmodeus, but fumble.  Asmodeus gets angry"...

So, true, he does telport away, and teleport back now and then to hit me 
twice.  But, with the Vorpal Blade, I get a critical hit by (at least) the
eighth time I hit him.  He dies.

In fact, I've killed four named demons so far, with my (relatively) wimpy
character (AC -15).  Doesn't seem like they're tough at all.

But without the Vorpal Blade, I might never kill them...


Just a thought...

